				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container>
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
					</div>
					<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"></div></div>
					
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-subjectpageheader">
</div><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha18" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Term in mathematics"}},"i":0}}]}'>Term in mathematics</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_matches_Wikidata"/></span>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"for","href":"./Template:For"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"complete intersection rings in commutative algebra"},"2":{"wt":"complete intersection ring"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt3" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt2" id="mwBA">For complete intersection rings in commutative algebra, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complete_intersection_ring" title="Complete intersection ring">complete intersection ring</a>.</div>
<p id="mwBQ">In mathematics, an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraic_variety" title="Algebraic variety" id="mwBg">algebraic variety</a> <i id="mwBw">V</i> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Projective_space" title="Projective space" id="mwCA">projective space</a> is a <b id="mwCQ">complete intersection</b> if the ideal of <i id="mwCg">V</i> is generated by exactly <i id="mwCw">codim V</i> elements. That is, if <i id="mwDA">V</i> has <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimension_of_an_algebraic_variety" title="Dimension of an algebraic variety" id="mwDQ">dimension</a> <i id="mwDg">m</i> and  lies in projective space <i id="mwDw">P</i><sup id="mwEA"><i id="mwEQ">n</i></sup>, there should exist <i id="mwEg">n</i> − <i id="mwEw">m</i> homogeneous polynomials:<sup about="#mwt4" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHarris1992136Definition_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEHarris1992136Definition"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEHarris1992136Definition-1"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Harris"},"2":{"wt":"1992"},"p":{"wt":"136"},"loc":{"wt":"Definition"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHarris1992136Definition-1" id="mwFA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<dl id="mwGA"><dd id="mwGQ"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt7" id="mwGg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"F_i(X_0,\\cdots,X_n), 1\\leq i\\leq n - m,"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle F_{i}(X_{0},\cdots ,X_{n}),1\leq i\leq n-m,}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>F</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>X</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>0</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mo>⋯<!-- ⋯ --></mo>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>X</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mn>1</mn>
        <mo>≤<!-- ≤ --></mo>
        <mi>i</mi>
        <mo>≤<!-- ≤ --></mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
        <mi>m</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle F_{i}(X_{0},\cdots ,X_{n}),1\leq i\leq n-m,}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/82a8e6c2a63402e989bb264d1ad821c6f2a283c2" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:31.521ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle F_{i}(X_{0},\cdots ,X_{n}),1\leq i\leq n-m,}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwGw">in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homogeneous_coordinates" title="Homogeneous coordinates" id="mwHA">homogeneous coordinates</a> <i id="mwHQ">X</i><sub id="mwHg"><i id="mwHw">j</i></sub>, which generate all other homogeneous polynomials that vanish on <i id="mwIA">V</i>.</p>

<p id="mwIQ">Geometrically, each <i id="mwIg">F</i><sub id="mwIw"><i id="mwJA">i</i></sub> defines a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypersurface" title="Hypersurface" id="mwJQ">hypersurface</a>; the intersection of these hypersurfaces should be <i id="mwJg">V</i>. The intersection of <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt8" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwJw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nowrap","href":"./Template:Nowrap"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;n&apos;&apos; − &apos;&apos;m&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>n</i> − <i>m</i></span> hypersurfaces will always have dimension at least <i id="mwKA">m</i>, assuming that the field of scalars is an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraically_closed_field" title="Algebraically closed field" id="mwKQ">algebraically closed field</a> such as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complex_number" title="Complex number" id="mwKg">complex numbers</a>. The question is essentially, can we get the dimension down to <i id="mwKw">m</i>, with no  extra points in the intersection? This condition is fairly hard to check as soon as the codimension <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt9" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nowrap","href":"./Template:Nowrap"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;n&apos;&apos; − &apos;&apos;m&apos;&apos;  ≥ 2"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>n</i> − <i>m</i>  ≥ 2</span>. When <span class="nowrap" about="#mwt10" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwLQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"nowrap","href":"./Template:Nowrap"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;n&apos;&apos; − &apos;&apos;m&apos;&apos; = 1"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>n</i> − <i>m</i> = 1</span> then <i id="mwLg">V</i> is automatically a hypersurface and there is nothing to prove.</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwLw" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwMA" aria-labelledby="Examples"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Examples">Examples</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Complete_intersection&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Examples"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwMQ">Easy examples of complete intersections are given by hypersurfaces which are defined by the vanishing locus of a single polynomial. For example,</p>
<dl id="mwMg"><dd id="mwMw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt11" id="mwNA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{V}(x_0^5 + \\cdots + x_4^5) = \\text{Proj}\\left(\\frac{\\mathbb{F}[x_0,\\ldots,x_4]}{(x_0^5 + \\cdots + x_4^5)}\\right) \\xrightarrow{i} \\mathbb{P}^4_\\mathbb{F}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {V} (x_{0}^{5}+\cdots +x_{4}^{5})={\text{Proj}}\left({\frac {\mathbb {F} [x_{0},\ldots ,x_{4}]}{(x_{0}^{5}+\cdots +x_{4}^{5})}}\right){\xrightarrow {i}}\mathbb {P} _{\mathbb {F} }^{4}}">
  <semantics>
