<p id="mwTg">Hence the twisted cubic is the projective scheme</p>
<dl id="mwTw"><dd id="mwUA"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt22" id="mwUQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\text{Proj}\\left( \\frac{R[x_0,x_1,x_2,x_3]}{(f_1,f_2,f_3)} \\right)."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\text{Proj}}\left({\frac {R[x_{0},x_{1},x_{2},x_{3}]}{(f_{1},f_{2},f_{3})}}\right).}">
